    "id": "fd_0131",
    "title": "Direction 2: Formal p-adic Completions and Valuation Theory",
    "description": "**Conjecture:** The p-adic numbers \u211a_p, formalized as the completion of \u211a with respect to the p-adic absolute value, satisfy all axioms of `ValuationIdeleData` when instantiated with the set of rational primes as places, and the diagonal embedding \u211a\u02e3 \u2192 \u220f_p \u211a_p\u02e3 lands in the restricted product with \u2124_p\u02e3 as integral subgroups \u2014 recovering the classical id\u00e8le group of \u211a.\n\n**Test:** Construct `ValuationIdeleData \u211a` using Mathlib's `Padic` and `PadicInt` types. Verify that `Padic.valuation` satisfies the multiplicativity and finite support axioms. Instantiate `principal_family_is_restricted` to obtain the classical theorem that every nonzero rational has non-trivial p-adic valuation at only finitely many primes.\n\nA disproof scenario: if Mathlib's `Padic.valuation` has incompatible normalization or type (e.g., valued in \u2124 vs. \u2115 vs. WithTop \u2124), the instantiation would require non-trivial adapter work.\n\n**Impact:** This connects our abstract algebraic framework to concrete number-theoretic objects, enabling formal proofs about actual number fields rather than abstract axioms.\n\n**Catalog References:** `LanglandsGL1/RestrictedProduct.lean` (ValuationIdeleData, principal_family_is_restricted)\n\n**Proof Strategy:** Use `multiplicity.Finsupp.finite` for the finite support condition. Adapt `Padic.valuation` to our \u2124-valued convention. Build a `ValuationIdeleData \u211a` instance.\n\n**Domain Bridges:** Algebraic number theory, p-adic analysis, valuation theory\n\n**Lineage:** Direct instantiation of `ValuationIdeleData` with concrete arithmetic.\n\n**Ambition:** \u2605\u2605\u2605\u2606\u2606 \u2014 Requires navigating Mathlib's p-adic infrastructure but mathematically straightforward.\n\n---",
